Plugins get the core's tab helpers, so a plugin route on an existing tab
(plugins/captcha, ./captcha-plugin) checks the caller's userId, serializes
with the core's own actions on that tab, and closes the tab when it overruns,
the way the core routes do.

diff --git a/server.js b/server.js
index 81dab76..292c27e 100644
--- a/server.js
+++ b/server.js
@@ -7299,6 +7299,13 @@ const pluginCtx = {
   destroySession,
   closeSession,
   withUserLimit,
+  // What a route on an existing tab needs (plugins/captcha): find the
+  // caller's tab, hold its lock, and close it when an operation overruns.
+  findTab,
+  withTabLock,
+  destroyTimedOutTab,
+  tabNotFoundResponse,
+  handleRouteError,
   safePageClose,
   createLeasedPage,
   closeLeasedPage,
